<title>DENMARK: DANISH MAY/JUNE RETAIL SALES UP 2.5 PERCENT Y/Y.</title>
<headline>DANISH MAY/JUNE RETAIL SALES UP 2.5 PERCENT Y/Y.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark's seasonally adjusted retail sales index fell to 112.40 in May and 112.50 in June compared to April's revised 113.20, the national statistics office said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>But compared to the same two months a year ago the combined figure showed a 2.5-percent rise, the office said.  </p>
<p>				    June 1997  May 1997  April 1997</p>
<p>  Seasonally adjusted volume  112.5	112.4     113.2*</p>
<p>  Food, beverages,tobacco     106.9	106.8     109.3*</p>
<p>  Clothing etc.		   117.0	114.3     114.1*</p>
<p>  Other consumer goods	  119.3	119.9     118.7*</p>
<p>* revised</p>
<p>NOTE - 1990 base = 100. Eight analysts polled by Reuters had forecast a seasonally adjusted average volume rise of 2.1 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>--Steve Weizman, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969652</p>
